{"sounds":{"intro":"Sindarin is the Grey-elven language invented by J. R. R. Tolkien for The Lord of the Rings. It has no native speakers. Tolkien left only a few hundred words and a few sentences, so it cannot be used for everyday talk. This pool contains only words and short phrases that appear in his own writings, with the spelling used in the books.","rows":[["dh","like \"th\" in \"this\"","edhel"],["th","like \"th\" in \"thin\"","thûl"],["ch","like \"ch\" in Scottish \"loch\"","ach"],["g","always hard, like \"go\"","galadh"],["c","always hard, like \"k\"","calen"],["r","rolled","ross"],["î / ê / â / ô / û","the vowel held long (the circumflex)","mîr"],["ae / ai / ei / au / ui","two vowels said as one sound","aran"]],"notes":["Words like \"mae govannen\" are real phrases from the books. Many others in fan lists are invented by fans and are not Tolkien's. Only words with a clear source are shown here.","This pool is much smaller than the Spanish one on purpose. A few forms are uncertain and nothing has been checked by an expert in Tolkien's languages. Treat it as a first guide for a hobby language."]},"numbers":[{"id":"1-to-10","title":"1 to 10","items":[["one","min","meen"],["two","tad","tahd"],["three","neled","NEH-led"],["four","canad","KAH-nahd"],["five","leben","LEH-ben"],["six","eneg","EH-neg"],["seven","odog","OH-dog"],["eight","tolod","TOH-lod"],["nine","neder","NEH-der"],["ten","pae","pye"]]}],"greetings":[{"id":"phrases-from-the-books","title":"Phrases from the books","items":[["well met","mae govannen","my go-VAH-nen"],["well done","mae carnen","my KAR-nen"],["I thank you","le hannon","leh HAH-non"],["thank you","hannon le","HAH-non leh"],["stop!","daro","DAH-ro"],["I am Legolas","im Legolas","eem LEG-oh-lahs"],["I desire","aníron","ah-NEE-ron"],["long live the halflings","cuio i Pheriain anim","KOO-yo ee FEH-ree-ine AH-neem"],["greeting","suilad","SOO-ee-lahd"]]}],"phrases":[],"vocab":[{"id":"people","title":"People","items":[["friend","mellon","MEL-lon"],["father","adar","AH-dar"],["mother","naneth","NAH-neth"],["brother","gwador","GWAH-dor"],["king","aran","AH-ran"],["elf","edhel","EH-thel"],["elves","edhil","EH-thil"],["man (human)","adan","AH-dan"],["men","edain","EH-dine"]]},{"id":"nature","title":"Nature","items":[["sun","anor","AH-nor"],["moon","ithil","ITH-il"],["star","gil","gheel"],["star (alt)","elen","EH-len"],["water","nen","nen"],["hill","amon","AH-mon"],["tree","galadh","GAH-lahth"],["land","dôr","dohr"],["fire","naur","NOWR"],["shadow","dae","die"]]},{"id":"things","title":"Things","items":[["city","ost","ost"],["tower","barad","BAH-rahd"],["gate","annon","AHN-non"],["home","bar","bar"],["jewel","mîr","meer"],["tongue / language","lam","lahm"]]},{"id":"colours","title":"Colours","items":[["green","calen","KAH-len"],["black","mor","mor"],["white","gwathren","GWAH-thren"],["red","caran","KAH-rahn"],["blue","luin","LOO-in"],["yellow","malen","MAH-len"]]}],"grammar":[{"id":"pronouns-and-possessives","title":"Pronouns and possessives","text":["The article \"i\" means \"the\". Plurals are usually made by changing the vowel: adan to edain (man), edhel to edhil (elf). This is called i-affection. \"Im\" is I. \"Le\" is you (polite). Possessives follow the noun: \"nîn\" (my) and \"lín\" (your)."],"rows":[["I","im","eem"],["you (polite)","le","leh"],["the","i","ee"],["my","nîn","neen"],["your","lín","leen"]],"ex":[["the man","i adan","ee AH-dan"],["the men","i edain","ee EH-dine"],["the elf","i edhel","ee EH-thel"],["the elves","i edhil","ee EH-thil"],["my friend","mellon nîn","MEL-lon neen"],["your friend","mellon lín","MEL-lon leen"]]}],"name":"Sindarin (Tolkien's Elvish)","id":"sjn","flag":"sjn","note":""}